REFERENCE
Glossary
HOS TRAINING  ·  Head Therapist Edition  ·  2 / 22
HOS
Human Operating System — the full framework treating the person as a high-performance system.
STIR
Stability · Tools · Internalization · Reflection — the four live dashboard variables.
M₁
Surface Mastery = S + T·I + R — current altitude / functional height.
M₂
Deep Capacity = S + T·I − R — structural depth after reflective load.
Circuit Breaker
If S + T < 5 → Safe Mode. No deep work until the system cools.
GRIT
Emotional-load ceiling = lowest STIR variable, mapped 0 → 0.5 → 1.0 → 1.5 → 2.0.
Safe Mode
Containment-only protocol: regulate, resource, stabilize — no processing.
Reflection Data
Every setback, loop, or drop is telemetry that improves the next flight.
Mismatch
A detectable pattern (e.g. High S + Low I) showing where the system is stuck.
Navigator
Integration stage: client owns tools, reactions, and direction — no longer a passenger.
