6-STEP PROTOCOL
Steps 1 – 3  ·  From Fire to Driver
HOS TRAINING  ·  Head Therapist Edition  ·  16 / 22
1
Get Out of the Building
Step Away from the Fire
Stop trying to “fix” or “analyze” the pain while you are being burned. Create immediate physical or mental distance. Get cool first. You cannot run logic on an overheated system.
2
Use the Ride
Therapy as Transportation
You are on the curb and don’t know the way yet. Let the therapist be the vehicle. They have the map and the keys for now. Use their office as a safe space to move away from the “trap house” of your past.

3
Take the Keys
Internalize the Tools

Watch how the driver handles the wheel. Start moving the coping skills and regulation tools from the therapist’s hands to your own. The goal is to move from “passenger” to “driver.”
6-STEP PROTOCOL
Steps 4 – 6  ·  From Observer to Navigator

HOS TRAINING  ·  Head Therapist Edition  ·  17 / 22
4
Look Through the Window

Revisit the Memory
Now that you are miles away and safe, look back at the old wounds. You are observing a “wilted rose” from a distance. You can see the facts of the story without breathing the smoke of the fire.
5
Expect the Wind to Change
Continuous Integration
Life will throw a “fickle breeze” your way. Triggers are not system crashes; they are routine updates. When the wind shifts, don’t turn the car around—just use your tools and keep driving.
6
New Address, New Life
Mastery
You have reached Integration. You own your head, your heart, and your reactions. The pain has been converted into insight. You are no longer “clean”—you are a Navigator.
