LANGUAGE
Client Translation — Tank Metaphors

HOS TRAINING  ·  Head Therapist Edition  ·  19 / 22
M₁ — Surface Mastery
“How full is the tank right now, and how well are you flying with what’s in it?”

Clients grasp altitude easily. High M₁ means they are functioning and reflecting well in the current conditions.
M₂ — Deep Capacity
“How strong is the tank itself once we subtract the energy spent reflecting and processing?”
This keeps the conversation honest: high reflection can inflate surface scores while structural capacity remains limited.
CULTURE
Shame-Proofing
HOS TRAINING  ·  Head Therapist Edition  ·  20 / 22
Setbacks = Reflection Data
In HOS there is no “failure.” Every drop in STIR, every tripped Circuit Breaker, every loop that didn’t climb is telemetry. The pilot does not get graded on turbulence; the pilot gets better instruments and better next-flight decisions.

